Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 2 20:45:53 2026 -0400

    skill: E6 V2 CUTOVER phase 4 — flip filename_suffix default to "" (#10685)
    
    The atomic-emit triple's filename_suffix default flips from ".v2.md"
    (pre-cutover §9a coexistence path) to "" (canonical CLAUDE.md path).
    This is the cutover moment: v2 outputs ARE the v1 paths now.
    
    Changes:
    - atomic_emit.assemble_and_emit: default filename_suffix=".v2.md" → ""
    - atomic_emit._atomic_write_triple: same
    - atomic_emit docstrings: rewrite to describe the post-cutover semantics
      (canonical default; .v2.md retained as explicit-suffix branch for
      legacy callers / coexistence-era tests)
    - compose.py deploy_alias_v2: docstring update for "first path is
      CLAUDE.md" (no longer .v2.md)
    - compose.py main() deploy --check + deploy-all --check: remove the
      DS-10685-phase2 F1 cutover-window WARNINGs added by Phase 2's fixup.
      Those warnings existed precisely to flag the phase-2-to-phase-4
      asymmetry; with phase 4 landing, the asymmetry is gone.
    - tests/test_atomic_emit_b7.py:
      - Update path assertions in 5 success/failure tests
        (CLAUDE.v2.md / CLAUDE.linked.v2.md / CLAUDE.conflicts.v2.md →
        CLAUDE.md / CLAUDE.linked.md / CLAUDE.conflicts.md)
      - Invert test_filename_suffix_default_is_v2 →
        test_filename_suffix_default_is_canonical (assert "" default)
      - Reframe test_filename_suffix_empty_writes_v1_canonical_paths into
        test_filename_suffix_v2_explicit_writes_legacy_paths (the .v2.md
        branch is now the opt-in for legacy callers, not the default)
      - Retire test_filename_suffix_v2_does_not_write_v1_paths — was a §9a
        coexistence guard ("v2 path must NEVER write v1 canonical
        filenames"); the cutover retires §9a, so this assertion is gone.
    
    Smoke: tests/test_atomic_emit_b7 + test_assemble_wired_b9 +
    test_compose_a2f_10492 + test_compose_a6_v2 + test_compose_check_a4_10388
    + test_compose_check_a45_10395 + test_b8_golden_assemble — 110 passed,
    1 skipped. Broader compose smoke (test_compose + 6 siblings) — 208
    passed, 1 failed (documented pre-existing
    test_event_driven_workflow_has_no_frontmatter, slated for Phase 5 D6).
    
    Remaining phases on branch: 3c (wizard.py migration) + 3d (delete
    deploy_role / _load_manifest / _resolve_includes / compose_role) — now
    unblocked since v2 writes to the canonical path. Then 3e
    (catalog_drift), 5 (D6), 6 (PRD docs), 7 (cumulative DS), 8 (squash PR).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

